    "created_at": "2024-04-30T14:25:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-04-30T14:25:09Z",
    "body": "> I'd also double check you really want `FrozenArray`. It uses rather dubious ES5 semantics and not as much is frozen as the name might lead you to believe. Generally I'd try to design APIs differently as to not require that.\r\n\r\nMy uninformed guess is that at least some of the specs use it as a way to make an attribute return some sort of array, as `sequence<T>` cannot be used as an attribute type. Do you mean reworking APIs so that they don't return make attribute getters return sequences or using a different type to represent the same thing?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
